Janis Papanagnou <Janis_Papanagnou@hotmail.com> writes:
> Topi Linkala wrote:
> > In that game the Magicbane was created when the wizard offerd a
> > corpse on a chaotic altar to her god. The Magicbane was created as a
> > chaotic artifact.
> > Now when it was found from the bones it was a neutral artifact.
> > Do you consider this as a bug. Shouldn't artifacts retain their
> > alignment in the bones file?
> 
> I don't think that it should have to retain its alignment ([1]) since
> bones are only loosely coupled with an actual game. The only problem I
> suspect is that another wizard might not be able to hold this wizard
> specific artifact from a bones file [2]. But either way couldn't that
> always be the case if a wizard finds it in a heap of bones before he
> gets it from his god?

No. The alignment of Magicbane in a given game is constant, and
depends entirely on the starting alignment and role of the character
that finds it, whether as a gift or in bones or by any other
means. For starting-chaotic Wizards, Magicbane will be chaotic; for
all other alignment-role combinations, it will be neutral.

